              "type": "text",
              "id": "AJ4vJ",
              "name": "Section note",
              "fill": "$mm-ink-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 900,
              "content": "The open detail area under an episode row (also used under a movie row). Full-width band in mm-surface-2 with the 3 px selection side bar continuing from the open row, one line under it, no shadow, no corners. Content starts at 136 px, the Title column of v2/Row/episode. Three sections, 24 px apart: Details (four v2/Fact/row in two columns), Versions (v2/Table/Header plus v2/Row/second-version rows, tracked version first) and History (v2/Table/Header plus v2/Row/history rows, newest first). Each section is a v2/Label/group heading 8 px above a white panel (mm-surface, 1 px mm-line, 8 px corners); the last row in a panel drops its line. History By and Detail line up with Versions Tracker and Seeding. Delete sits only in the Action column of a second version. States, as instance overrides: open and selected (default); open, not selected (Side bar off); one version (second version row off); no history yet (history rows off, Empty text on); second version downloading (Seeding cell shows the live pill, Delete off). Code: TanStack Table row expansion (getCanExpand, row.getIsExpanded, row.toggleExpanded) renders this as the expanded row content: a shadcn TableRow with one TableCell spanning every column; the Versions and History panels are shadcn Table elements inside it.",
